## Summary

Closes #328.

This F4 / CAP-123 slice adds a privacy-safe, restart-durable operator boundary for degraded OTP delivery health:

- candidates are derived only from aggregate OTP delivery health `ATTENTION` and `CRITICAL` snapshots;
- equal or greater recent severity suppresses duplicate candidates inside a configurable cooldown;
- `ATTENTION -> CRITICAL` escalation is recorded immediately;
- candidate evaluation runs only after a final delivery health event is durably appended;
- candidate persistence failure cannot replace provider semantics or trigger another provider send;
- candidate and acknowledgement rows are immutable and bounded by retention;
- acknowledgement is separate, idempotent and stores only server-derived Admin actor/time;
- no free-text acknowledgement is accepted;
- acknowledgement requires dedicated `OPERATIONAL_ALERT_ACKNOWLEDGE`, recent step-up and same-session CSRF;
- Publisher remains read-only while Reviewer and Access Admin may acknowledge;
- acknowledgement explicitly does not mean remediation, recovery, resolution or incident closure;
- consumer/mobile APIs remain unchanged; Admin API changes are additive and aggregate-only.

## Contract-first evidence

- ADR-0116 — Durable OTP alert candidates and Admin acknowledgement;
- `docs/contracts/otp-delivery-alert-candidates.v1.json`;
- linear migration `20260806_0033` after `20260805_0032`;
- executable alert-candidate contract checker;
- composable parent OTP delivery-health and HTTP-delivery checkers;
- memory cooldown, escalation, privacy and idempotency tests;
- secured Admin capability, CSRF, step-up and exact-confirmation tests;
- PostgreSQL restart, concurrency, retention, schema and UPDATE-rejection tests;
- additive Operational Reports OpenAPI overlay and exact composed OpenAPI gate;
- dedicated `OTP Delivery Alert Candidates CI`;
- durable F4 checkpoint.

## Exact-head verification

Exact runtime head: `c67acd8eb07cfd626ad4480d55e67370bbba7a63`

