The dedicated alert workflow proves migration, restart durability, advisory-lock concurrency, cooldown deduplication, immediate escalation, idempotent acknowledgement, bounded retention, aggregate-only schema, direct UPDATE rejection and parent identity/privacy regressions.

## Verification corrections

- The first cooldown test waited 31 minutes while the health window was 15 minutes, so the older failures had correctly expired. The test-only cooldown was changed to 5 minutes and the repeat was moved to minute 6, remaining inside the health window. Runtime policy and behavior were unchanged.
- A temporary bootstrap initially wrote full runtime OpenAPI into the stable base snapshot, causing an overlay schema collision. The parent base blob was restored and only the additive Operational Reports overlay was generated. Temporary bootstrap workflows were removed; `openapi.v1.json` has no final PR delta.
- The parent OTP HTTP checker required the exact error-registry version `1.21.0`. It now enforces a minimum version of `1.21.0`, allowing the additive `1.22.0` registry while preserving the required OTP error registrations.

All final evidence above belongs to `c67acd8eb07cfd626ad4480d55e67370bbba7a63`.

## Evidence boundaries

This PR does not provide or prove:

- external paging;
- email, SMS or Slack operator notification;
- incident-management integration;
- automated remediation or recovery;
- provider delivery receipts or callback authenticity;
- real email/SMS deliverability;
- production threshold quality;
- deployed alert latency, availability or SLO behavior;
- operator response effectiveness;
- an operator-executed incident or rollback drill.

Acknowledgement means only that an authorized Admin operator observed the candidate. It is not incident resolution or provider recovery.

