## LOT B3.4.4 — Dedup & Change Detection

### Scope
Classify canonical partner rows as `invalid`, `new_property`, `new_offer`, `update_offer`, `duplicate` or `manual_review` without creating or publishing anything.

### Changes
- deterministic property fingerprint from city, neighborhood, type, rounded surface and bedrooms;
- deterministic offer fingerprint from property identity, transaction, stable reference and rounded price;
- stable-reference update detection;
- same-property/different-offer classification;
- ambiguity routed to manual review;
- all decisions remain `publication_eligible=false`;
- dedicated tests, documentation, migration report and CI gate.

### Production state
The Supabase connector blocked the report migration through its safety control. No bypass was attempted. Therefore the migration is present in code but not claimed as applied in production.

### Non-effects
- no real partner data;
- no property/offer/listing creation;
- no automatic merge;
- no search or ranking mutation;
- no publication.
